limpet-tools (0.1.2) unstable; urgency=low

  * Populate the wq#4086 `limpet-kb` creds category (wq#4087):
    DefaultCreds-Cheat-Sheet (MIT, 3767 rows) and ics-default-passwords
    (MIT via SecLists, 107 rows, reshaped to the vendor/product/username/
    password/protocol columns kb-sources.d/ics-default-passwords.toml
    already declared) populate /usr/share/limpet/kb/creds/, and a new
    many-passwords.toml source (GPL-2.0, 2860 rows) is added alongside
    them. Each CSV ships with its upstream .LICENSE file; provenance in
    limpet/kb/creds/SOURCES.md. `limpet-kb update && limpet-kb search
    <query> --category creds` now returns real results.

 -- Lumen Industries <packaging@lumen.local>  Sat, 17 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000

limpet-tools (0.1.1) unstable; urgency=low

  * Fix systemd unit packaging (wq#4071): rename the unit source to
    debian/limpet-tools.limpet-registry-daemon.service and pass
    --name=limpet-registry-daemon to dh_installsystemd. The 0.1.0 .deb shipped
    the daemon binary with no unit (empirically confirmed with
    dpkg-buildpackage; dh_installsystemd silently skipped the bare file).

 -- Lumen Industries <packaging@lumen.local>  Fri, 16 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000

limpet-tools (0.1.0) unstable; urgency=low

  * Initial packaging of the limpet plugin-registry CLI (limpet/cli.py) and
